      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve: warn before non-ClawHub plugin installs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a gap where users could install plugins from npm, git, local paths, local archives, npm-pack tarballs, or marketplace sources without a clear install-time acknowledgement that the source is outside ClawHub review and trust metadata.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a distinct non-ClawHub provenance acknowledgement path for plugin installs while leaving ClawHub release-risk acknowledgement, `security.installPolicy`, and lifecycle `before_install` hooks intact. ClawHub installs continue without the non-ClawHub warning; non-ClawHub CLI, deprecated hooks alias, and Crestodian-approved install flows now forward the explicit acknowledgement state.\n\nMerge order note: this is the OpenClaw-side warning step and should land after the ClawHub dependency-scanning/trust-metadata step unless maintainers choose a different order.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInteractive users now see a warning before installing from sources that are not ClawHub-reviewed. Noninteractive users can proceed only after explicitly passing `--acknowledge-non-clawhub-install`, making automated installs intentional and auditable.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Non-ClawHub install sources now emit an outside-ClawHub-review warning and require prompt/flag acknowledgement before installer side effects.\n- Explicit ClawHub installs do not show the non-ClawHub warning and keep their separate ClawHub risk acknowledgement behavior.\n- Deprecated `openclaw hooks install` and approved Crestodian plugin installs forward the new acknowledgement flag instead of bypassing the install-time warning path.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `git diff --check` passed before and after commit.\n- `pnpm docs:list` passed.\n- Focused Testbox run covering plugin install, hooks alias, and Crestodian operation tests passed: 196 tests.\n- Testbox `check:changed` passed.\n- `codex review --uncommitted` completed clean with no concrete correctness, security, or maintainability regressions found.\n",
        "branch": "jesse/non-clawhub-untrusted-installs",
        "head_sha": "2bb480b6bf3ca1461b89ce8d6ead6f73f79910f7",
